  "verbalization": "Thiotepa, a chemotherapy agent, is implicated in the treatment of B-cell Neoplasm through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Thiotepa is associated with Mantle Cell Lymphoma, a type of B-cell neoplasm, and that this condition is further linked to drugs like Acalabrutinib, Lenalidomide, and Bortezomib, all of which are indicated for B-cell Neoplasm. These findings collectively imply that Thiotepa may exert a therapeutic effect on B-cell neoplasms through mechanisms that are not yet fully understood, possibly involving the modulation of cellular pathways or immune responses. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Thiotepa in the treatment of B-cell neoplasms, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence underscores the importance of considering the broader therapeutic context in which Thiotepa is used, as its relationship with B-cell neoplasms appears to be mediated through a chain of drug-indication links.",
